Currently: "found no match for symbol 'clear'".  Round-84 diagnosis
CORRECTION: the candidate IS the element's clear(enum); what fails is
type-checking the enum-name-qualified ARGUMENT (et::B) -- fargs is
starved and the arity mismatches.  The failure is STATEFUL: a fresh
re-typecheck of the same argument (after one failed attempt) succeeds
and the whole TU then converts (crashing later in symex
assign_from_struct -- a further layer).  A retry inside the argument
loop did NOT reproduce that recovery; root cause in the qualified-
enumerator resolution's lazy scope creation is still open.  Bare
enumerators and direct (non-operator->-rewritten) calls work.
